<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly unchanged on Wednesday, mirroring the trend at the overnight money market, traders said.</p>
<p>Only the one-month rate was lower. The six-month rate was slightly up due to adjustments by some banks, a trader said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks would be willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 26		 FEB 25</p>
<p>    1 W		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/16		10  1/8</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10  3/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  3/8		 10  5/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/2		 10  1/2</p>
<p>    VAL		27-Feb		  26-Feb</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
